  "metadata": {
    "note": "Annual growth rate of India's working-age population (aged 15-64). Still positive but slowing steadily, from about 2.5% in 2000 to under 1% by 2030 and roughly zero by 2049, turning negative in 2050. The broad 15-64 pool is still expanding, a beat behind the youth cohort (which already shrinks, Fig 2.2.C), but its growth is fading too: the demographic tailwind has a clear end date. A few projection years (2025, 2026, 2032) are absent in the source workbook and omitted here. Source: World Bank, The Global Jobs Challenge (2026), Figure 2.3.B (India line); UN WPP 2024.",
    "sourceLine": "World Bank, The Global Jobs Challenge (2026 advance edition). CC BY 3.0 IGO.",
    "figure": "2.3.B",
    "zeroBaseline": true
  }
